# UST.G3BG Root-Tube Primitive Projection and Explicit Period-Shift Theorem

## Result

G3BF reduces the Deligne computation to the pairing-four root tube before any
odd-meridian search. G3BG now identifies the exact primitive source vector that
must be transported.

The B83 integral K3 model contains two hyperbolic planes with
`e_i^2=f_i^2=0` and `e_i.f_i=1`, and fixes

```text
H=e1+f1,
delta=e2-2f2,
gamma=f2.
```

Thus

```text
H^2=2,
delta^2=-4,
H.delta=0,
delta.gamma=1.
```

For a divisor `D`, projection to the primitive lattice `H^perp` is

```text
pr_Hperp(D)=D-(D.H/H^2)H.
```

Since `Rminus=H-delta` and `H.Rminus=2`,

```text
pr_Hperp(Rminus)=Rminus-H=-delta.
```

Therefore the primitive class of the G3BF root tube is not an unknown dense
vector. It is exactly

```text
z_4=-delta tensor u_B=(-e2+2f2) tensor u_B.
```

It has two nonzero coordinates in the local rank-42 source model and satisfies

```text
<delta tensor u_A,z_4>=-delta^2=4.
```

## Explicit period shift

The G3BB-selected pairing-one dual is

```text
z_1=gamma tensor u_B=f2 tensor u_B.
```

The difference entering the G3BF Deligne multiplication law is therefore

```text
k=z_4-4z_1
 =(-delta-4gamma) tensor u_B
 =(-e2-2f2) tensor u_B.
```

Its source pairing vanishes exactly:

```text
<h_Z,k>=4-4=0.
```

Hence `k` lies in the integral vanishing kernel and

```text
R_B(z_4)-4R_B(z_1)=Pi_C(T_Z(k)).
```

The replacement-period ambiguity is now an explicit two-coordinate ambient
class, not an unspecified element of a rank-1509 lattice.

## Computational consequence

The next calculation no longer starts by guessing or reconstructing a dense
root vector. Its exact input is

```text
(-e2+2f2) tensor u_B
```

in the rank-42 ambient primitive lattice. The open map is its integral
transgression into the fixed B89 rank-1509 marking, followed by the 248-row
normalized readout.

This also sharpens the optional G3AU descent test. The only replacement shift
that must be tested is

```text
(-e2-2f2) tensor u_B.
```

No full arbitrary period-shift search is needed for this root representative.

